From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: enable wakeup-source on the EC node

Uncomment wakeup-source on the Huawei Gaokun EC I2C node so the I2C core marks
the EC interrupt as a wakeup source, allowing charger plug/unplug and lid
events to wake the system from s2idle.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index 8e82061..a2c3453 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -732,8 +732,8 @@
 		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 173 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		bat-gpios = <&tlmm 41 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
-		// not stable yet, so comment out it
-		// wakeup-source;
+		/* EC events, such as plugging in a charger, wake the system. */
+		wakeup-source;
 
 		pinctrl-0 = <&ec_default>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
